But this is the approximation for small angles, and 2π/13 ≈ 0.483 is not that small. The actual value is 0.0133, which is less than the approximation 0.0564, because the higher-order terms reduce it.

Anyway, for equal spacing, the minimum is the same for all consecutive triples. For non-uniform spacing, some triples would have smaller area. So equal spacing is optimal for maximizing the minimum on a circle.

